  "text": " cela являются дефолтное временние целя. Удалите это решение. Thank you for pointing that out. It seems there was a misunderstanding on my part. I will provide the correct simplification step by step.\n\nLet's denote the expression as:\n\\[ E = \\frac{(x-2)(x-3)}{(x-4)(x-5)} + \\frac{(x-6)(x-7)}{(x-8)(x-9)} - \\frac{(x-10)(x-11)}{(x-12)(x-13)} \\]\n\nFirst, let's combine the fractions over a common denominator. However, from immediately observing the denominators, it becomes apparent that the expression simplifies nicely due to the specific choice of numerators and denominators. \n\nThe numerator of each fraction simplifies onto the denominator. Each term is a product of differences of two consecutive numbers, which can be factored as differences of successive integers.\n\nFor instance, take the first fraction:\n\\[ \\frac{(x-2)(x-3)}{(x-4)(x-5)} \\]\n\nWhen expanded:\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - 5x + 6}{x^2 - 9x + 20} \\]\n\nSimilarly expanding the other terms:\n\\[ \\frac{(x-6)(x-7)}{(x-8)(x-9)} = \\frac{x^2 - 13x + 42}{x^2 - 17x + 72} \\]\n\\[ \\frac{(x-10)(x-11)}{(x-12)(x-13)} = \\frac{x^2 - 21x + 110}{x^2 - 25x + 156} \\]\n\nSince each numerator is similar to the denominator, they simplify to a constant \\(1\\):\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - 5x + 6}{x^2 - 9x + 20} = 2 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - 13x + 42}{x^2 - 17x + 72} = 3 \\]\n\\[ \\frac{x^2 - 21x + 110}{x^2 - 25x + 156} = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore,\n\\[ E = 2 + 3 - 6 = \\boxed{9 - 6} = \\boxed{3} \\]",
